1. GPL-3 notice for pando-tts
-----------------------------
pando-tts statically links sherpa-onnx, which contains espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later) and the
piper-phonemize glue. The pando-tts binary is therefore distributed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version (licenses/GPL-3.0.txt).
The Corresponding Source of pando-tts is published at the same place and release tag as the
binary; see SOURCE-OFFER.md. You may replace pando-tts with your own build: the app uses the
program configured in its settings and only warns, never refuses, when it differs.
The app and pando-stt contain no espeak-ng code (checked at release time with
`cargo xtask check-nm`).

2. Engines and runtimes
-----------------------
- Whistle STT: weights `whistle.cact` (Cactus Compute, Apache-2.0, repo Cactus-Compute/whistle,
  commit ca5287601bef25af26dcf2e1b2bdc0843a7c19e5) and the needle engine `libneedle.a`
  (Cactus Compute, Apache-2.0 licence tag; distributed as a prebuilt static library, engine
  source not published, repo Cactus-Compute/needle3, commit 93e88ede867e4311c39151285e74df513e4b835b).
  Linked into pando-stt only. Licence text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
- sherpa-onnx 1.13.8 (k2-fsa, Apache-2.0) in pando-tts (with TTS) and optionally in pando-stt
  (built from source with SHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_TTS=OFF).
- ONNX Runtime (Microsoft, MIT), bundled inside sherpa-onnx.
- espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later), piper-phonemize (MIT): pando-tts only. espeak-ng-data/ files
  shipped next to the voices are part of that GPL work.
- Silero VAD v5 (snakers4, MIT), optional model for pando-stt.
- GPUI / GPUI Kit (gpui-pre, gpui-kit, Apache-2.0), sonora (BSD-3-Clause), cpal (Apache-2.0).

